{"seq":null,"source_sha256":"33334968fe34c87719682c0567426876d98b442189d1cbf1cacbe6ef13bcbb39","commit_to":{"owner":"teamwork-inc-test","repo":"e2e-team-repo","branch":"e2e-662-team-20261009043208"},"doc_stem":"2026-10-09-1-seed-team-20261009043208","status":"completed","machine":{"spec_version":8,"spec_hash":"48411dad1f94"},"checkpoint":"navigate","run_id":"mp-eng-48ad35fa","payload":{"expand_iris":[],"focus":"November 1, 2026 operational changes: Priya Holm’s fortnightly intake rota with 15-minute hand-off calls, and Dario Kent’s pantry shelf restock threshold of one-third full","rationale":"I checked the thematic and document doors: the only narrative area is Anti-Slack product positioning, while the two listed documents concern context preservation and real-time chat; their spans do not overlap this rota or pantry policy. The people door yielded no entries and Unplaced is empty. I deliberately leave those product-positioning materials and unrelated positions unexpanded because none bears on these operational changes.","n8n_execution_id":"158700","expansion_count":0,"context":"# Perspective — teamwork-inc-test/e2e-team-repo @ d072ee3e1ce7a43ff43841eca7624550f822d399\npin: e7438bd9623ee5a61b6fc518aee2808c4ea1738d\n\nSections: (1) THE MAP — this graph's richest ground, full narration; (2) COVERAGE — what's active, contested, unplaced, and quiet across everything else, meaning inside whisper-brackets; (3) DOORS — complete axes (areas, people, dimensions, documents, unplaced), each one expand away; (4) FOCUS — material loaded for your focus, LAST. The map, coverage, and doors never vary with your focus.\n\n^-marked entries are compressed stubs carrying child addresses. Their narration and any surfaced witness quotes are verbatim-accurate — quote them as-is — but a stub carries no provenance (source, date, supersession). Expand (aswritten_expand with the IRIs you need) before any claim that turns on WHEN or by WHOM something was said, or whether it is still the current framing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nThis entry is BOUNDED — the whole graph is deliberately not inlined. Every node is reachable within a bounded number of expands: before concluding the perspective is silent on your subject, check the map and coverage, then expand the door whose axis would hold it (^Thematic for topics and areas, ^People for anyone, ^Documents for a call or memory, ^Unplaced for loose positions). Absence becomes signal only after the relevant door shows nothing.\n\n# The map — this graph's richest ground (top fidelity band)\n\n## ^Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning  [4 children · 20260310]\nTanya frames the product against Slack's real-time model. The anti-Slack label is the primary positioning thesis: every conversation should produce a persistent decision artifact.\n  decisions-under 1 · evidence 4 — expand ^Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning for the full child index\n\n# Coverage — narrated, from four directions\n\nActive: [ Position_ContextPreservationNextSprint · Next sprint focus: context preservation — linking decisions to t… ^Position_ContextPreservationNextSprint ] · [ Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat · Real-time chat (Slack, Teams) is the named anti-pattern. The pro… ^Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat ] — the newest witnessed work, one document each.\n\n# Doors — pick an axis\n\n[ ^Thematic — every area (0) by name ] [ ^People 0 ] [ ^Dimensions — 0 axes ] [ ^Documents 2 ] [ ^Unplaced 0 ]\nEach door expands to a complete axis: aswritten_expand(iris=[\"Thematic\"]) — same coords as this perspective. Nothing in the graph is outside every door.\n\n# Focus: November 1, 2026 operational changes: Priya Holm’s fortnightly intake rota with 15-minute hand-off calls, and Dario Kent’s pantry shelf restock threshold of one-third full (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### StyleMetrics_Sprint4Retro\ntype: StyleMetrics\nwitnessed: 20260322\nsource: Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\nProfessional-operational register. High active voice ratio driven by direct executive quotes and imperative framing. Low jargon density — technical terms (webhook, hash-based dedup, Zephyr) are product/engineering terms used precisely. Short punchy sentences alternate with longer attributed quotes.\nunder: StyleMetrics\n\n### Position_Sprint4ThesisProven\ntype: Position\nwitnessed: 20260322\nsource: Sample_Sprint4Retro_20260322\nTanya: 'This sprint proved the thesis.' The widget intercepts the moment of consensus in any chat thread and creates a persistent decision record with full context, requiring zero extra steps.\nunder: PositioningThesis, Narrative_ZeroEffortCapture\n\n### Position_PricingTwelveDollars\ntype: Position\nwitnessed: 20260310\nsource: Sample_TeamworkProductVision_20260310\nPricing set at $12/user/month as of 2026-03-10 product vision session. Note: Sprint 4 retro (2026-03-22) records a pricing update to $15/user for teams over 25.\nunder: Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning, PackagingEntitlement\n","positions":"","pin":"e7438bd9623ee5a61b6fc518aee2808c4ea1738d","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[]}","context_bytes":3837},"live_run_id":"a315231e1ccf","at":"2026-10-09T04:33:46Z"}
